999
M7.1 release fixture (M7 spec 22, Fixture A + Fixture B combined): a rectangle
999
carrying two explicit LINEAR dimensions.
999

999
THE GEOMETRY IS DELIBERATELY WRONG. It is drawn 99.5 x 49.7, its bottom side
999
rises 0.0497 over its run (about 5e-4 rad off horizontal), and the closing side
999
misses the origin by 0.0005. All three errors are INSIDE the reconstruction
999
tolerances, which is what Fixture B is for: if the drawing were already
999
100 x 50 and square, an implementation that reconstructed nothing would pass
999
every assertion, and the gate would be measuring this file instead of the code.
999

999
The DIMENSIONS state 100 and 50 (group code 42). Reconstruction believes the
999
stated value over the drawn one -- they differ by 0.5% and 0.7%, well inside
999
the agreement band -- so the SOLVER is what moves the geometry to 100 x 50.
999

999
Analytical oracle after reconstruction and a 20 mm pad:
999
  100 x 50 x 20 = 100000 mm^3
999
and after Width 100 -> 120:
999
  120 x 50 x 20 = 120000 mm^3
999

999
The anonymous *D1 / *D2 BLOCKS below hold the arrows and witness lines every
999
real dimensioned DXF carries. They are here ON PURPOSE: ADR-M6-009 says block
999
contents are not model geometry, and importing them would add eight stray lines
999
to a four-line rectangle. Their presence is what makes that guard testable.
